✅ Theory for Gradient Descent Algorithm
✅ 1. Introduction

Gradient Descent is an optimization algorithm used to find the minimum value of a function.
It works by moving step-by-step in the direction opposite to the gradient (i.e., downhill), because the gradient points toward the direction of maximum increase.

This algorithm is widely used in:

Machine learning

Deep learning

Mathematical optimization

✅ 2. Concept Behind Gradient Descent
✅ Why Gradient?

The gradient of a function tells us:

which direction increases the function value

how steep the slope is

To find the minimum, we want to move in the negative direction of the gradient.

